    {
      "id": "GFG-02",
      "chapter": "lifts",
      "anchor": "lifts-gram-fibre-overlap",
      "title": "Continuous test integrals glue the measures pointwise",
      "statement": "On the open set of invertible Hermitian targets, support, the regular-locus disintegration identity and continuity of compactly supported test integrals uniquely determine the family at every target. It extends by zero off that set.",
      "hypotheses": "The tuple and Hermitian target spaces are locally compact, second-countable Hausdorff Borel spaces. Haar measure on the target is positive on nonempty open sets. Tests in the continuity condition have compact support contained in the regular source.",
      "correspondence": "Overlap uniqueness is obtained from equal integrals on compact subsets. A countable subcover split into disjoint measurable pieces proves disintegration, and multiplication by a target cutoff gives continuity. The circle example distinguishes ordinary almost-everywhere disintegration from pointwise agreement.",
      "dependencies": [
        "GFG-01"
      ],
