      "title": "The ratio of source and target Haar scalings fixes each regular fibre",
      "statement": "Changing μ and ν to aμ and cν with a,c>0 changes the unique Gram-fibre measure at each regular target by a/c.",
      "hypotheses": "The regular Gram-fibre theorem applies to the original source and target measures, and the scale factors are positive finite reals.",
